# plans/pr-review-boards-2026-09-22-phase-4-plan.md P4-T07 (FEA-24) · UX-SPEC.md §Board ("Card
# detail") · DESIGN-SYSTEM.md §6 (`CardTile::reference`) · TESTING-HARNESS.md §3 — a review card
# says which pull request it is about, on the tile and in the detail.
#
# The `reviews` preset (§4) puts one card on the context's Reviews board through
# `UpsertPullRequestCard`, the request a review schedule's run sends, naming `acme/api#1`. It
# sits in Reviewed, so nothing runs on it and the column is the third one: two `l` from Pending
# review.
#
# Two projections say it:
#   `board.cards`       a row's badges are the card's key, then the pull request's
#                       `owner/name#number` — the text the tile's `reference` slot draws.
#   `card.properties`   the detail's property column, where the `Pull request` row follows
#                       Worktree and reads `acme/api#1 · open ↗`.
#
# `B` (open) and `y` (copy) are not driven here: one launches the developer's browser and the
# other needs a clipboard no lane has (§1). Both are pinned by the gpui tests in
# `screens/board/actions.rs`.
#
# No `shot`: this is a keyboard scenario, so it runs in the headless lane too (§7).
fixture: reviews
await idle 30000
key g p
await hub_tab == Prs 15000
key tab
await key_contexts[2] == "Board" 20000
await lists.board.rows[2].label == "Reviewed" 20000

# The card is on the tile with its pull request beside its key.
key l l
await lists.board.selected.label == "Reviewed" 10000
assert lists["board.cards"].rows[0].label == "Review the retry budget"
assert lists["board.cards"].rows[0].badges[0] == "REV-1" && lists["board.cards"].rows[0].badges[1] == "acme/api#1"

# `⏎` opens the card, and its property column carries the `Pull request` row under Worktree.
key enter
await dialog.name == CardDetail 15000
assert lists["card.properties"].rows[8].label == "Worktree"
assert lists["card.properties"].rows[9].label == "Pull request" && lists["card.properties"].rows[9].badges[0] == "acme/api#1 · open ↗"
assert lists["card.properties"].rows[10] absent
key escape
await dialog absent 10000
assert key_contexts[2] == "Board"
quit
